// lib/data/seed_consumables.dart
//
// Genuine CONSUMABLE items only -- filtered from the full CDA Admin / CDA Ops
// inventory spreadsheets (cda_admin.xlsx, cda_ops.xlsx) down to items that are
// actually consumed during daily operations and have a short useful life
// (purchased for use, not long-term ownership), per this definition:
//   Batteries, Propellers, Drone motors (frequently replaced), Screws/nuts/bolts,
//   Electrical wires & connectors, Adhesives (glue/epoxy), Lubricants,
//   Cleaning materials, Printer paper, Ink cartridges, Pens & markers,
//   Cable ties, Solder wire & flux.
// Fixed/durable assets (furniture, drones, cameras, tools, logbooks, files,
// storage boxes/trays, appliances, etc.) from the source sheets were excluded.
//
// NOTE ON THE 'branch' FIELD:
// Each item's 'branch' holds the display label ("CDA Admin", "CDA Ops", or
// "CDA Ops & CDA Admin" for items shared across both) and is written straight
// through to Firestore's 'branch' field by ConsumableService.seedConsumables()
// -- this is also exactly what the branch filter chips in ConsumableListScreen
// compare against. Do not rename this field.
//
// 'category' holds the specific consumable type ("Batteries", "Propellers", etc.)
// so the category filter chips in ConsumableListScreen -- which are built
// dynamically from whatever's loaded -- show these groupings automatically.

